    "narrative": "The Austin Waves face a favorable schedule today, headlined by a high-upside matchup against Spence. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** leads our positional output with a 74.56 efficiency score; hitting second against a 6.03 xERA arm provides the perfect storm for a multi-hit day. **Kyle Tucker** remains our most reliable anchor despite the mid-order placement, boasting a 75.38 score that prioritizes his high floor even against Martinez. Meanwhile, **Curtis Mead** and **Nasim Nunez** are in prime spots to exploit Spence\u2019s inefficiency, with **Curtis Mead**\u2019s 63.58 score bolstered by his premium #3 slotting, while **Nasim Nunez** maintains high value despite his #9 placement due to the sheer volume of plate appearances he is projected to see against a struggling rotation.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision involved **Cole Carrigg**, who just barely missed the optimal threshold at 55.71. He fell behind the likes of **Jacob Wilson** and **Nolan Schanuel** because he is currently tasked with facing Imanaga, one of the more difficult left-handed assignments on the board. While **Cole Carrigg** brings necessary speed, his matchup against a sub-4.00 xERA arm capped his ceiling today. On the injury front, the absence of **Luis Robert Jr.** and **Jordan Westburg** continues to shorten our depth, and with **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** and **Gunnar Henderson** scheduled for an off-day, the bottom of our lineup is currently relying on stream-adjacent players like **Nolan Schanuel** to maintain our competitive edge in AVG. We are monitoring the weather closely for the game involving **Liam Hicks**, as any unexpected delay against Wheeler would be particularly punishing given his already tight 45.31 projection.",
